Tara Venkataraman: quick post-mortem from today's "tooling" breakout: several folks hit confusing behavior trying to stream a function_call with json_mode while rolling their own retry. Errors ranged from 'Extra data after top-level value' to the SDK returning a partial array.
Noah Li: share the minimal repro? is this using the official SDK or a lightweight wrapper?
Tara Venkataraman: official JS SDK but the app adds a custom fetch retry that replays the same request object on 401. Example pattern in the sample repo (simplified):
```js
const make = async () => {
  try {
    return await client.responses.create({ model:'redwood-chat-1', json_mode:true, function_call:{name:'log_event', arguments_schema:evSchema}, input });
  } catch (e) {
    if (isAuthErr(e)) { await auth.refresh(); return await client.responses.create({...}); }
    throw e;
  }
}
```
Grace Park: yep that's the pattern we tell people to avoid. Two failures: (1) the incremental parser keeps state across the retry so the second stream becomes appended to the old buffer -> extra data error, (2) if the model was streaming an array, the SDK might return the valid prefix silently which looks like a successful short result.
Noah Li: does this happen in Py too? parity matters for bootcamp.
Tara Venkataraman: Py historically re-instantiates parser per connection so it avoided the concat issue, which made JavaScript look broken during demos. We should call this out.
Grace Park: short-term fixes we agreed on in the breakout: (a) update the bootcamp sample to use idempotency_key for streaming endpoints, (b) add a troubleshooting FAQ blurb showing how to reset parser state before retrying, (c) show the safer helper usage example.
Tara Venkataraman: long-term SDK work: expose a high-level helper `createStreamSafe` that by default does three things: injects idempotency_key if not provided, resets parser state on retry, and surfaces raw_fragment + parse_offset when a streaming parse fails. That reduces onboarding friction.
Noah Li: API sketch I like:
```js
await client.responses.createStreamSafe({
  model:'redwood-chat-1',
  json_mode:true,
  function_call:{ name:'report_issue', arguments_schema:issueSchema},
  retry_policy:{ max_attempts:3 },
  expose_raw_on_error:true
});
```
It should also emit lightweight telemetry events like `parser_reset_on_retry` when that code path triggers.
Grace Park: agree on telemetry. helps us correlate workshop crashes to retry behaviour and environment (RN EventSource, corporate proxies, etc.).
Tara Venkataraman: other UX improvements we discussed:
- `parseOrRaw()` helper so beginners can get raw text when the schema validator fails instead of an opaque crash
- `schema_coerce` flag in samples to show how to permissively accept numbers/strings for prototyping
Noah Li: we should not enable `schema_coerce` by default in the SDK, but samples can show it as an onboarding escape hatch. And provide clear warnings in the README.
Grace Park: RN caveat: EventSource polyfills can interleave non-JSON keepalive/comment lines or HTML auth pages on reconnect. Suggest SDK streaming adapters support `sse_strip_comments:true` and a `resetOnReconnect:true` option. Bootcamp mobile sample will opt into those.
Tara Venkataraman: small implementation notes for whoever picks this up: the parser reset should be cheap (dispose parser objects, clear buffers) and happen before the retry request is re-attached to the stream. Also add a deterministic unit test that simulates: mid-stream 401 => auth refresh => retry frames arriving as a second stream.
Noah Li: I'll file one ticket for the helper + tests and another for docs + sample updates. Naming proposals: DEVEX-1600 `createStreamSafe` + DEVEX-1601 `bootcamp: streaming retry patterns`.
Docs Bot: New issues created: DEVEX-1600 - "createStreamSafe: idempotency + parser reset + diagnostics" and DEVEX-1601 - "bootcamp samples: update streaming retry patterns and RN adapter notes". Links: https://jira.redwood.ai/browse/DEVEX-1600 , https://jira.redwood.ai/browse/DEVEX-1601 :white_check_mark:
Grace Park: quick PR plan: Noah picks SDK helper + tests, I will update the bootcamp sample to use the helper and add a short FAQ entry. Tara will update the live slides and include a one-slide troubleshooting checklist.
Tara Venkataraman: thanks all. this will stop at least two demo catastrophes in future sessions. :tada:
